# Privacy Policy: PagePocket

**Last updated: October 2026**

## Overview

PagePocket is a Chrome extension that saves web pages as PDF, PNG or JPEG files, or copies them to your clipboard. This policy explains how it handles your data.

## Data collected

**PagePocket does not collect, send or share any personal data.** Nothing ever leaves your device.

When you pocket a page, the extension takes screenshots of the current tab (or redraws it), builds the file in your browser and saves it to your Downloads folder. Page content and screenshots are never stored by the extension or sent anywhere.

## Data stored on your device

PagePocket keeps a small amount of information in Chrome's local extension storage, on your device only:

- **Your settings**: capture mode, file format, method and quality
- **Your pocket counter**: how many pages you have saved, used for fun milestone badges
- **Recent pockets**: the file names, formats and Chrome download IDs of your last 5 saves, so you can open them with "Show"

This information is never sent anywhere. You can clear it at any time by removing the extension.

## Data sharing

No data is collected, transmitted or shared with any server, service or third party. All processing happens locally using bundled open-source libraries (html2canvas and jsPDF).

## Permissions

- **activeTab**: temporary access to the current tab, only when you click PagePocket, use the right-click menu or the keyboard shortcut
- **scripting**: scrolls the page during capture, hides repeating sticky headers, and runs the Quick render library
- **downloads**: saves the file to your Downloads folder and opens it with "Show"
- **storage**: keeps your settings, counter and recent pockets on your device
- **contextMenus**: adds "Pocket this page" to the right-click menu
- **offscreen**: a hidden extension page that stitches screenshots together and builds the file, so capture keeps going if you close the popup

